codex
1. What changed

I patched the `event-fast*` benchmark paths to respect an explicit `wallMs: 0` while keeping the existing `2000`ms default when `wallMs` is omitted. The change is limited to:
[engine-fast-worker.js](/C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773516738208-29584/js/app/engine-fast-worker.js#L275)
[engine-fast-par-worker.js](/C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773516738208-29584/js/app/engine-fast-par-worker.js#L398)
[engine-fast-par-host.js](/C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773516738208-29584/js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js#L678)

2. Which verification I ran

I ran a focused local Node check against the edited code paths and confirmed:
`wallMs: 0 -> 0`
missing `wallMs -> 2000`
negative `wallMs -> 0`

I also ran the fact-sim engine test harness with `reruns=0` and `strictFinalParity=false`:
`engine_test(action="run", engines=["event-fast-worker","event-fast-par"], examples=["simple"], maxWallMs=1, targetSimMs=1000, maxLoops=100, realStepMs=16, stopOnFirstFailure=true)`
Result: `PASS`, 6/6 cases passed, no issues. The tool would not accept `maxWallMs=0`, so the exact zero-duration case was verified locally instead.

3. Residual risk

Residual risk is low and isolated to the zero-duration benchmark edge case. The main limitation is that the MCP engine test API rejects `maxWallMs=0`, so the exact runtime integration for that value was not exercised end-to-end through the harness, but the patched logic was verified directly in all three affected files.
